<title>GERMANY: DASA 1996 sales preliminary 13 bln DM.</title>
<headline>DASA 1996 sales preliminary 13 bln DM.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG said its sales in 1996 rose to a preliminary 13 billion marks ($7.7 billion) from 11.5 billion marks the year before.</p>
<p>Incoming orders rose to 16.9 billion marks from 10.9 billion marks, while profit was substantially better, said chief executive Manfred Bischoff, without naming specific profit figures.</p>
<p>The workforce fell to 44,936 from 46,892, and should fall further to 42,500 this year, Bischoff said.</p>
<p>Sales are expected to rise about six percent this year to 14 billion marks, Bischoff said. The company should be further strengthened by its portfolio restructuring, he said.</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150 ($ = 1.680 German Marks)</p>
